{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".macro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s library declares the macro, the same kind, and the read of the set. It depends on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets and re-exports it, because the expansion calls LinkerSets’ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"users’ files:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")","","extension Endpoints {","    public static var all: [Endpoint] {","        LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its users then register routes and read them through the library:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = Endpoints.all"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the re-export exposes","anchor":"What-the-re-export-exposes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let home = ..."},{"type":"text","text":" expands, in the user’s file, to one call:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Routes.home)"},{"type":"text","text":". That macro, which LinkerSets declares,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expands in turn to the record itself, one declaration per object format, naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":". So the user’s file has to see LinkerSets. With"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import LinkerSets"},{"type":"text","text":" in the client’s library, importing the client is enough. With a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public import"},{"type":"text","text":", every user’s file fails to compile with “no macro named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” until it imports LinkerSets itself. The compile tests in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/CompileFailures"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExportingClientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUserImportingLinkerSets"},{"type":"text","text":") check each case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So every file that imports the client also sees "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" and anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"public the client adds to them. A kind constant doesn’t need to be public: the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"kind as a number, so users’ files never name the constant. Keep it internal and give users the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values through the client’s own API, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Endpoints.all"},{"type":"text","text":" does above. A user can still read the set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by its number, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)"},{"type":"text","text":"; an internal constant only keeps it out of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"autocomplete and out of the client’s public API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the same record "},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes, in the same section, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute ("},{"code":"'@Route' applies to static members only","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Registering types","anchor":"Registering-types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record then holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", read with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Any.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Checking keys are unique","anchor":"Checking-keys-are-unique"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can give each declaration a key that no other record of its kind in the same executable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or library may share, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKey(of:attribute:)","isActive":true},{"text":". The expansion then adds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function whose symbol is named for the kind and the key, and a second declaration with the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key fails to compile in one module, or to link across modules:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func uniqueKey(of declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol, attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> String? {","        declaration.asProtocol(NamedDeclSyntax.self)?.name.text","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro whose users write the key returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKeyArgument(of:)"},{"text":", which reads a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey:"},{"text":" string literal. An empty key, and a key on a member of a private type, are refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with diagnostics of their own. A macro whose users declare same-named types in private scopes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/UniqueKeyInPrivateScope\/omitted"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKeyInPrivateScope"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and such a record is written without its key. The check reaches one linked image only; LinkerSets’ guide to unique","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keys shows each linker’s message and the limits.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Declaring the kind once","anchor":"Declaring-the-kind-once"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin returns the kind from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and the library reads the set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, so the number appears twice, and a mismatch shows only at run time, as an empty set. To write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it once, put it in a module of its own that depends on nothing, and have both import it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ RoutesKind","public enum RouteKind {","    public static let rawValue: UInt32 = 0x726F_7574  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ RoutesMacros, the plugin","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { RouteKind.rawValue }","}"]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Routes, the library","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: RouteKind.rawValue)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package lists the module among both targets’ dependencies:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro(name: \"RoutesMacros\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", ...])"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".target(name: \"Routes\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", \"RoutesMacros\", ...])"},{"type":"text","text":". SwiftPM builds it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the host for the plugin and for the target for the library."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Writing records without depending on LinkerSets","anchor":"Writing-records-without-depending-on-LinkerSets"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" depends on LinkerSets, which builds LinkerSets’ own plugin,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSetsMacros, and swift-syntax with it. A module that only writes a few records, such as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events of one feature, can skip that. A client with a plugin of its own declares two macros there:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an entry macro that takes the kind as an argument, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" does, and a record macro"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its own under a different name, which the entry macro’s expansion calls in place of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ DiscoveryMacros, the plugin","@main","struct DiscoveryMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [DiscoverableMacro.self, DiscoverableRecordMacro.self]","}","","public enum DiscoverableMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) throws -> UInt32 {","        try kindArgument(of: attribute)","    }","","    public static var recordMacroName: String { \"discoverableRecord\" }","}","","public enum DiscoverableRecordMacro: DeclarationMacro {","    public static func expansion(","        of node: some FreestandingMacroExpansionSyntax,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try LinkerSetRecordMacro.expansion(of: node, in: context)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares both and re-exports LinkerSetsRuntime, whose names the record uses:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Discovery, the library","@_exported import LinkerSetsRuntime","","@attached(peer)","public macro Discoverable(kind: UInt32) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableMacro\")","","@freestanding(declaration)","public macro discoverableRecord<Value>(kind: UInt32, storing value: Value) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableRecordMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that writes records then depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Discovery"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime"},{"type":"text","text":", not on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets, and writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Discoverable(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"type":"text","text":" where it would have written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"type":"text","text":". Its build holds the client’s plugin, which already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs swift-syntax, and not LinkerSetsMacros. The record macro’s name must differ from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", because a module that imports both LinkerSets and the client couldn’t choose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between two macros of the same name."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Testing the expansion","anchor":"Testing-the-expansion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client’s expansion tests pin one line per record, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" call:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["assertMacroExpansion(","    \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        @Route","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","    }","    \"\"\",","    expandedSource: \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","","        #linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Endpoints.home)","    }","    \"\"\",","    macroSpecs: [\"Route\": MacroSpec(type: RouteMacro.self)],","    failureHandler: { Issue.record(\"\\($0.message)\") }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"assertMacroExpansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" expands only the macros in its table, so the call stays as written, and it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads the same on every swift-syntax from 600 on. The record behind it, one declaration per object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, belongs to LinkerSets and changes when LinkerSets adds a format. A test that wants it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anyway adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"linkerSetRecord\": MacroSpec(type: LinkerSetRecordMacro.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the table. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration at file scope expands to the call inside a private enum of its own, whose name comes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the context’s unique names (","type":"text"},{"code":"__macro_local_15linkerSetRecordfMu_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Writing the expansion yourself","anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" supplies the peer ","type":"text"},{"code":"expansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from it for the record. That’s how","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event struct Login {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only its metatype, read as "},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first. It returns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" says why, and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is where to report it, or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the declaration can hold a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other refusal still reaches ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the expansion.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A member declared in an extension of a generic type is refused only when the extension shows the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type is generic: by naming generic arguments (","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Box<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension [Int]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"where","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" clause. A plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Box","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"code":"struct Box<T>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads like an extension of any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type, because the macro sees the extension’s syntax and not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Box","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s declaration. No refusal is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned for it, and the compiler fails inside the expansion with “static stored properties not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supported in generic types”. A client macro whose users might write one can say so in its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"docs.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMa